/////////acceptance criteria


AC1 – Supported Phone Fields
Given a Contact record is created or updated through the Snowflake integration
When phone data is received by Dynamics 365
Then only the following Contact fields shall be evaluated and standardized:

Business Phone (Telephone1)
Home Phone (Telephone2)
Mobile Phone (MobilePhone)
And no other Contact phone-related fields shall be modified as part of this enhancement.

AC2 – E.164 Storage Standard
Given a value is received for Telephone1, Telephone2, or MobilePhone
When the Contact record is created or updated
Then the stored value shall be converted to E.164 format.

And the stored value shall follow the pattern:




Plain Text
+<CountryCode><PhoneNumber>
``
Show more lines
Examples

Incoming Value	Stored Value
123-456-7890	+1234567890
(123) 456-7890	+1234567890
506-7123-4567	+50671234567
AC3 – Removal of Non-Numeric Characters
Given a phone number contains formatting characters
When the integration processes the phone number
Then all formatting characters shall be removed, including:

Spaces
Hyphens (-)
Parentheses ()
Periods (.)
Any other non-numeric characters
And the resulting value shall be stored in E.164 format.

AC4 – North American Country Code Handling
Given the Contact Country is United States or Canada
And the phone number does not already contain a country code
When the phone number is processed
Then the system shall automatically prepend country code "1".

Example

Country	Incoming Value	Stored Value
US	2245221234	+12245221234
Canada	4165551234	+14165551234
